## Story Description
Enhance dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py with two new analytical sections and cross-filtering on the top-suppliers chart. The cross-filter uses on_select so clicking a supplier bar in the top-20 chart filters the monthly trend and category/BU bars to show only that supplier's data. New sections added at the bottom of the page: Category x Business Unit heatmap (7x7 spend intensity matrix) and Opportunity Prioritisation scatter (each category as a bubble: x=total_spend, y=unique_supplier_count, size=transaction_count). The existing _top_suppliers function is modified to emit selections and return selected supplier names.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — add import: from dashboard.components.charts import horizontal_bar, donut_chart, scatter_bubble (scatter_bubble is new, horizontal_bar and donut_chart are already imported; update the existing import line accordingly).
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — change signature of _top_suppliers to _top_suppliers(filtered: pd.DataFrame) -> list[str]. At the end of the function, change st.plotly_chart(fig, use_container_width=True) to: event = st.plotly_chart(fig, on_select='rerun', key='overview_top_suppliers', use_container_width=True). Then: points = (event or {}).get('selection', {}).get('points', []); selected = [p['y'] for p in points if 'y' in p]; if selected: st.caption(f'Cross-filter active: {", ".join(selected[:3])} — click chart background to clear'); return selected.
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — add function _category_bu_heatmap(filtered: pd.DataFrame) -> None. Guard: if filtered.empty or 'category_l1' not in filtered.columns or 'business_unit' not in filtered.columns: st.info('No category x BU data available.'); return. Compute: pivot = filtered.groupby(['category_l1','business_unit'])['base_amount'].sum().unstack(fill_value=0). Build: import plotly.express as px; fig = px.imshow(pivot, color_continuous_scale='Blues', aspect='auto', title='Spend by Category x Business Unit (AUD)', text_auto='.3s'). Apply: fig.update_layout(paper_bgcolor='white', font=dict(size=11), xaxis_title='Business Unit', yaxis_title='Category'). Render: st.plotly_chart(fig, use_container_width=True).
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — add function _opportunity_scatter(filtered: pd.DataFrame) -> None. Guard: if filtered.empty or 'category_l1' not in filtered.columns: st.info('No data.'); return. Compute: agg = filtered.groupby('category_l1').agg(total_spend=('base_amount','sum'), supplier_count=('canonical_supplier_name','nunique'), txn_count=('transaction_id','count')).reset_index(). Filter: agg = agg[agg['supplier_count'] >= 2]. Rename columns to match scatter_bubble args: agg.rename(columns={'category_l1':'Category','total_spend':'Total Spend (AUD)','supplier_count':'Supplier Count','txn_count':'Transaction Count'}, inplace=True). Call: fig = scatter_bubble(agg, x='Total Spend (AUD)', y='Supplier Count', size='Transaction Count', color='Category', label='Category', title='Opportunity Prioritisation: Spend vs Supplier Fragmentation'). Add annotation: fig.add_annotation(text='High spend + many suppliers = consolidation opportunity', xref='paper', yref='paper', x=0.01, y=1.08, showarrow=False, font=dict(size=10, color='grey')). Render: st.plotly_chart(fig, use_container_width=True).
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — in main(), apply cross-filter. Change the call to _top_suppliers(filtered) to: selected_suppliers = _top_suppliers(filtered). After that line, add: cf = filtered[filtered['canonical_supplier_name'].isin(selected_suppliers)] if selected_suppliers else filtered. Then change the calls to _spend_by_month and _category_and_bu to use cf instead of filtered.
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py — in main(), after the existing _pareto_and_donut section and before _quality_scorecard, add: st.markdown('---'); st.subheader('Category x Business Unit Intensity'); _category_bu_heatmap(filtered); st.markdown('---'); st.subheader('Opportunity Prioritisation'); _opportunity_scatter(filtered).
- Run: PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) python3 -m py_compile dashboard/pages/01_spend_overview.py && echo 'syntax OK'

